<p>In 2016, University of Buenos Aires computer science student Gonzalo Ciruelos worked out that <a href="https://gciruelos.com/what-is-the-roundest-country.html">the roundest country in the world is Sierra Leone</a>, with a roundness index of 0.934 on a scale of 0 to 1.</p>
<p>He&#8217;d been inspired by David Barry, who&#8217;d found that <a href="https://pappubahry.com/misc/rectangles/">the world&#8217;s most rectangular country is Egypt</a> (0.955 on the same scale).</p>
<p>Metropolitan France is known as the Hexagon. I suppose each country has its claim to fame.</p>
<p>(Gonzalo Ciruelos, &#8220;What Is the Roundest Country?&#8221;, <em>Math Horizons</em> 26:3 [February 2019], 26-27.)</p>
